    <briefdescription>
<para>Multiplexer for GraphQL subscriptions with topic-based filtering. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Manages multiple concurrent GraphQL subscriptions on a single WebSocket connection, applying topic filters and rate limiting to each subscription.</para>
<para>Core components:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>SubscriptionFilter</computeroutput>: Topic/attribute selector for filtering events</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>SubscriptionMultiplexer</computeroutput>: Per-connection state for multiple subscriptions</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Subscription lifecycle:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Client sends <computeroutput>subscribe</computeroutput> message with query and filters</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Multiplexer validates subscription and stores filter state</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>On change event from Changefeed: multiplexer applies filters</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Matching events sent to client as <computeroutput>next</computeroutput> messages</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Client sends <computeroutput>complete</computeroutput> → subscription canceled</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Filter types:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Topic-based: match entity type and operation (e.g., &quot;users:create&quot;)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Attribute predicates: key-value matching (e.g., {&quot;status&quot;: &quot;active&quot;})</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Complex: boolean combinations (AND, OR, NOT)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Performance:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Filter matching is O(n) where n = number of active subscriptions</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Suitable for moderately high concurrency (10s-100s of subscriptions)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bounded memory via max_subscriptions config</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><heading level="3">Thread safety</heading>
</para>
<para><computeroutput>SubscriptionMultiplexer</computeroutput> is thread-safe. Event publishing and subscription management may be called concurrently from different threads.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>0.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Maturity: 🟢 PRODUCTION-READY </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Score: 86/100 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Status: Production Ready </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
